<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Themed (monochrome) launcher icon.

  Android's themed icons keep only the ALPHA channel of this drawable and tint it
  with the user's wallpaper palette. The adaptive foreground could not be reused
  for that: its leaf is an opaque white shape carrying dark veins and green
  glands, so its alpha is one solid filled blob and the silhouette is lost.

  Two rules make this one work, and both are violated by a naive copy of the
  coloured vector:

  1. ONE colour, fully opaque. A second colour brings its own alpha, and the
     foreground's 0.96 leaf fill against its 1.0 glands is invisible to the eye
     but becomes a hole once only alpha survives.
  2. Detail as NEGATIVE space, never as lighter paint. The veins are cut out of
     the leaf with evenOdd rather than stroked in a paler colour, which would be
     tinted exactly like the leaf and vanish.

  The outline is the same leaf as the adaptive foreground, so the two icons stay
  recognisably the same mark. The leaf body and the veins live in one even-odd
  path: covered once it paints, covered twice it does not. Every vein is strictly
  inside the outline, so nothing depends on a subpath touching the boundary, and
  the whole thing degrades to a plain solid leaf if a renderer ever ignores the
  fill type.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Leaf body, then the veins cut out of it. -->
    <path
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:fillColor="#FF000000"
        android:pathData="M54,34 C61,29 70,36 71,47 C72,58 66.5,69.5 58,76.5 C55,78.8 53,83.5 54,88 C55,83.5 53,78.8 50,76.5 C41.5,69.5 36,58 37,47 C38,36 47,29 54,34 Z
            M54,80 L56,66 L56,50 L54,42 L52,50 L52,66 Z
            M54.33,58.13 L44.83,49.13 L43.17,50.87 L52.67,59.87 Z
            M53.67,58.13 L63.17,49.13 L64.83,50.87 L55.33,59.87 Z
            M54.38,69.18 L47.88,62.18 L46.12,63.82 L52.62,70.82 Z
            M53.62,69.18 L60.12,62.18 L61.88,63.82 L55.38,70.82 Z" />
</vector>
